Follow the pipeline in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — design before code, and stop and ask if a
request contradicts a documented convention.

Before editing anything here, read
[docs/conventions/40-frontend.md](../../docs/conventions/40-frontend.md).

The three that are most often got wrong:

- **A CRUD screen is a config object in `src/entities/`, not a page file.** Writing a page component
  that lists records with add/edit/view/delete means you took the wrong path.
- A new screen needs a menu row in `apps/server/seed/index.js`, or it is invisible to every
  non-admin user and resolves to all-false permissions.
- Use semantic Tailwind tokens (`text-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `text-fg-quaternary`) and merge with
  `cx` from `@/utils/cx`. Raw colours break dark mode. There is no `tailwind.config.js` — the theme
  is CSS-first in `src/styles/theme.css`.

Never edit `src/components/base/` or `src/components/application/` — vendored Untitled UI. Wrap them
in `src/components/ui/` instead.
